{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00397",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.88,
      "end_seconds": 5.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.27,
      "end_seconds": 9.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.68,
      "text": "Great. Hello, come in and sit down. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.79,
      "end_seconds": 15.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "It's pain in my right ankle. I thought I'd wait, but it hasn't gone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 17.0,
      "end_seconds": 19.66,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "How long has this been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.03,
      "end_seconds": 25.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "For about a week, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 27.29,
      "end_seconds": 31.55,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.0,
      "end_seconds": 41.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.41,
      "text": "Pretty mild, if I'm being honest. I notice it more with walking. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 42.06,
      "end_seconds": 44.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "So, anything that tends to go along with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 45.83,
      "end_seconds": 47.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "It usually comes with swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.22,
      "end_seconds": 53.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.87,
      "text": "I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 53.19,
      "end_seconds": 58.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.33,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.31,
      "end_seconds": 61.21,
      "duration_seconds": 1.9,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 62.6,
      "end_seconds": 71.39,
      "duration_seconds": 8.79,
      "text": "As for swelling, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 72.33,
      "end_seconds": 75.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.49,
      "text": "Is it constant, or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.54,
      "end_seconds": 83.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.7,
      "text": "It's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.56,
      "end_seconds": 88.31,
      "duration_seconds": 4.75,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.76,
      "end_seconds": 90.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "It happens all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.15,
      "end_seconds": 94.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "And how severe is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.38,
      "end_seconds": 101.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.4,
      "text": "Well, it's... hard to say, it's kind of... I don't know—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.15,
      "end_seconds": 106.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.63,
      "text": "Take your time. Mild, moderate, or severe, if you had to pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.35,
      "end_seconds": 108.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.38,
      "text": "Moderate, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.5,
      "end_seconds": 113.99,
      "duration_seconds": 4.49,
      "text": "Alright, any fever, pop or crack, numbness or pain in the knee?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.33,
      "end_seconds": 125.09,
      "duration_seconds": 9.76,
      "text": "No, no fever, no pop or crack, no numbness. I did have difficulty walking at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.35,
      "end_seconds": 130.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "And pain at the back of the heel, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 130.74,
      "end_seconds": 134.06,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "No. No pain at the back of the heel."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 136.87,
      "end_seconds": 139.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Okay, and your skin, any changes there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 140.54,
      "end_seconds": 142.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 144.14,
      "end_seconds": 152.15,
      "duration_seconds": 8.01,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. BP is 113 over 68, heart rate 78, temperature is 36.8 degrees, SpO2 98 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.64,
      "end_seconds": 157.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.79,
      "text": "Okay, noted. Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.97,
      "end_seconds": 161.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.12,
      "end_seconds": 168.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else? I'm asking so that we don't miss anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.36,
      "end_seconds": 179.49,
      "duration_seconds": 10.13,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.72,
      "end_seconds": 183.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "Sorry, the computer needs a moment to load this."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.72,
      "end_seconds": 185.44,
      "duration_seconds": 0.72,
      "text": "No rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 193.73,
      "end_seconds": 199.09,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. Right, anyone in the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.39,
      "end_seconds": 204.52,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "My mother had high blood pressure. My grandmother had breast cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.89,
      "end_seconds": 211.81,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.27,
      "end_seconds": 219.52,
      "duration_seconds": 7.25,
      "text": "Allopurinol, 100 milligrams, once a day for the gout. It's amlodipine, 5 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 220.04,
      "end_seconds": 224.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Doctor, our chart from the last visit lists it as 2.5 milligrams."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.85,
      "end_seconds": 229.1,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Hm, that's different. Is the latest prescription anywhere near you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.74,
      "end_seconds": 233.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.48,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.56,
      "end_seconds": 241.07,
      "duration_seconds": 6.51,
      "text": "It's a... um, you know, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.02,
      "end_seconds": 244.37,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Alright, do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.27,
      "end_seconds": 261.13,
      "duration_seconds": 15.86,
      "text": "For the heart rhythm, I believe. My wife sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night for my cholesterol. I'd been on losartan, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.07,
      "end_seconds": 263.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.9,
      "end_seconds": 268.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Yes, I had a C-section, about ten years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.02,
      "end_seconds": 271.35,
      "duration_seconds": 1.33,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.07,
      "end_seconds": 273.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "I don't drink at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 277.54,
      "end_seconds": 280.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.09,
      "end_seconds": 283.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.93,
      "text": "I've had gout, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.54,
      "end_seconds": 285.24,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 285.76,
      "end_seconds": 287.45,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Yes, high blood pressure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.58,
      "end_seconds": 289.31,
      "duration_seconds": 0.73,
      "text": "I see."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 290.5,
      "end_seconds": 301.01,
      "duration_seconds": 10.51,
      "text": "An irregular heartbeat, for five years. High cholesterol, for five years. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. I've never really been one for hospitals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.6,
      "end_seconds": 305.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Sorry about the noise outside, the building work never stops."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 306.67,
      "end_seconds": 308.7,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "I hadn't even noticed, honestly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.42,
      "end_seconds": 314.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.43,
      "text": "Okay, I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.77,
      "end_seconds": 316.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Okay, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.67,
      "end_seconds": 320.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Breathe in deeply... and out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 333.85,
      "end_seconds": 338.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.9,
      "text": "The bones themselves aren't tender and the ankle feels stable when I test it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 339.28,
      "end_seconds": 339.98,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 340.89,
      "end_seconds": 343.21,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "Now I'm going to check this part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 355.1,
      "end_seconds": 360.07,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "There's swelling and bruising on the outer side of the ankle, tender over the ligament."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.67,
      "end_seconds": 386.35,
      "duration_seconds": 21.68,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. Okay, so my impression is this: It fits best with an ankle sprain. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer. A ligament tear is also on my list."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 387.17,
      "end_seconds": 396.72,
      "duration_seconds": 9.55,
      "text": "Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had pain in your right ankle for about a week, mild, and no pop or crack or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.79,
      "end_seconds": 399.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 399.5,
      "end_seconds": 404.21,
      "duration_seconds": 4.71,
      "text": "I'm going to order an X-ray of the ankle, for ankle injury."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0068",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 405.49,
      "end_seconds": 408.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "I can book that for Monday at 2 pm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0069",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 408.89,
      "end_seconds": 434.99,
      "duration_seconds": 26.1,
      "text": "I'll start you on paracetamol, 650 milligrams, three times a day, for three days. You take it by mouth. That's for ankle pain. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Rest, ice for twenty minutes at a time, a compression bandage and keep the foot up. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0070",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 436.02,
      "end_seconds": 437.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Okay, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0071",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 438.04,
      "end_seconds": 456.14,
      "duration_seconds": 18.1,
      "text": "If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department. I'd like to see you again in ten days. Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0072",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 456.78,
      "end_seconds": 465.66,
      "duration_seconds": 8.88,
      "text": "So, I take the paracetamol, 650 milligrams, three times a day and come back in ten days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0073",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 466.12,
      "end_seconds": 471.13,
      "duration_seconds": 5.01,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Wonderful, I think that's it. Ask me anything before you go."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0074",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 472.71,
      "end_seconds": 475.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.21,
      "text": "No, I think that's everything. Thank you, doctor."
    }
  ]
}